步骤1 – 确定每个22秒的爆裂量

\[
\begin{aligned}
t_1 &= 22\ \text{s},\qquad N_1 = 80\ \text{粒}
t_2 &= 22\ \text{s},\qquad N_2 = 3N_1 = 3\times80 = 240\ \text{粒}
t_3 &= 22\ \text{s},\qquad N_3 = 7N_1 = 7\times80 = 560\ \text{粒}
t_4 &= 22\ \text{s},\qquad N_4 = \frac{N_1}{2} = \frac{80}{2} = 40\ \text{粒}
\end{aligned}
\]

**步骤2 – 计算总的爆裂量**

\[
\begin{aligned}
N_{\text{total}} &= N_1 + N_2 + N_3 + N_4 \\
&= 80 + 240 + 560 + 40 \\
&= 920\ \text{粒}
\end{aligned}
\]

**步骤3 – 考虑剩余热的爆裂**

在最后22秒之后，40%的剩余粒子仍然会爆开。

\[
\begin{aligned}
N_{\text{remaining}} &= N_{\text{total}} - N_4 \\
&= 920 - 40 \\
&= 880\ \text{粒}
\end{aligned}
\]

\[
\begin{aligned}
N_{\text{remaining}} &= \frac{4}{5}N_{\text{remaining}} \\
\frac{1}{5}N_{\text{remaining}} &= 880 \\
N_{\text{remaining}} &= 880 \times 5 = 4400\ \text{粒}
\end{aligned}
\]

**步骤4 – 最终的爆花数量**

\[
\begin{aligned}
N_{\text{total}} &= N_{\text{total}} + N_{\text{remaining}} \\
920 &= 920 + 4400 \\
4400 &= 0
\end{aligned}
\]

因此，在4400个粒子中，只有920个是由于火的爆裂而产生的。

\[
\boxed{920}
